'''La Serra de Llevant''' ({{lang|ca|La Serra de Llevant}}; "Eastern Mountain Range") is a [[comarca]] in the far eastern highlands of [[Tramuntana Province]], [[Balboa]]. It is the easternmost comarca in the province, encompassing the upper watersheds of the [[Yalabirga River|Yalabirga]] system on the Shendan-facing slope of the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] range, including [[Lake Iwarakí]] and the surrounding highland valleys. The comarca capital is [[Vila de Llevant, Tramuntana|Vila de Llevant]], situated on the eastern shore of Lake Iwarakí, and the largest settlement is [[Sant Jorge, Tramuntana|Sant Jorge]], located approximately 40 kilometres north of the lake along the Sant Jorge River valley. The comarca had a population of 25,000 in 2026.

La Serra de Llevant is one of the most sparsely populated and remote comarcas in Balboa. The terrain is rugged montane highland, with steep ridges and forested slopes rising above narrow valley floors. The comarca's economy is dominated by the operation of the [[Gran Presa del Nord]], a major hydroelectric dam on the southern shore of Lake Iwarakí operated by the [[Corporació Hidroelèctrica de Balboa]] (CHB), which is the primary employer in the comarca. The area is home to a significant [[Birú people|Birú]] population, and the comarca has been a focal point of indigenous rights activism and opposition to infrastructure development on traditional lands.

== Etymology ==

The name ''La Serra de Llevant'' (Volisanian for "Eastern Mountain Range") refers to the comarca's location on the eastern highlands of Tramuntana Province, along the Yalabirga range. The name distinguishes the comarca from the western highland comarcas of the province and reflects the Volisanian colonial administrative division of the Tramuntana highlands. The indigenous Birú name for the region is not widely documented; the Birú toponymy of the area is preserved primarily in the names of individual features, including [[Lake Iwarakí]] and the Yalabirga range itself.

== Geography ==

La Serra de Llevant occupies the far eastern highlands of Tramuntana Province, along the Shendan-facing (western) slope of the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] range. The comarca is bounded by the [[La Taula]] comarca to the northwest, by the highland interior of Tramuntana Province to the west and south, and by the border with [[Nurra Province|Nurra]] to the east. The terrain is rugged montane highland, with elevations ranging from approximately 800 metres in the valley floors to over 1,500 metres along the ridgelines. The Yalabirga range forms the eastern boundary of the comarca, separating the Shendan-facing slope from the Aethiopian-facing watershed of Nurra Province.

The comarca's principal geographic feature is [[Lake Iwarakí]], a reservoir lake covering an area of 704.586 km² at an elevation of approximately 850 metres. The lake was originally a natural freshwater lake formed in a glacial valley basin and was converted into a regulated reservoir with the construction of the [[Gran Presa del Nord]] dam at its southern outflow in the 1970s. The lake is fed by the Sant Jorge River and several smaller highland streams draining the surrounding ridges, and its outflow is regulated by the dam into the [[Yalabirga River]].

The climate is cooler than the coastal lowlands, with a pronounced wet season from May to November that brings the majority of the comarca's rainfall. The Shendan-facing slope lies in the rain shadow of the higher Yalabirga peaks to the east, resulting in drier conditions than the Aethiopian side of the range. Annual rainfall in the comarca ranges from approximately 1,000 to 1,500 mm, supporting montane forest vegetation on the slopes and limited agriculture in the valley floors.

The limestone formations on the eastern slope of the Yalabirga range contain a network of caves that are sacred to the [[Birú people|Birú]] and have been used for ceremonial purposes for centuries. The caves are among the most significant indigenous cultural sites in the Tramuntana highlands and have been a source of conflict between Birú communities and infrastructure projects, most notably during the [[2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest]].

=== Settlements ===

The comarca's settlements are concentrated in the highland valleys and along the [[E8 expressway (Balboa)|E8 expressway]], the primary road link across the northern highlands. The two principal settlements are:

